==Latin==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|ine-pro|la}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*ḱn̥s-eh₁-}}, {{term/t|ine-pro|*ḱn̥s-eie-||to announce}}. Cognate with Sanskrit {{term|शंसति|tr=śaṃsati||to declare|lang=sa}}, Avestan {{term|tr=sąh-|||to speak solemnly|lang=ae}}.{{rfscript|ae}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Classical}} {{IPA|/ˈkeːn.se.oː/|lang=la}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|censeo|cēnseō|censere|cēnsēre|censui|cēnsuī|censum|cēnsum}}

# I give an [[opinion]].
# I [[think]], [[suppose]] or [[judge]].
# I [[recommend]].
#:''Ceterum '''censeo''' Carthaginem esse delendam''
# I [[decree]], [[vote]] or [[determine]].
# I [[count]] or [[reckon]].
# I [[assess]].

